# Cloud pricing

Storage + usage, never seats — the slider where the stack scales but the bill is honest. The anti-seat-pricing stance made tangible.

client :pricing do
  <section id="cloud-pricing">
    <div class="cp-inner">
      <p class="cp-kicker"><span class="dot"></span>the cloud · pricing</p>
      <h2 class="cp-h">Pay for storage and usage.<br>Never for seats.</h2>
      <p class="cp-sub">Most teams rent a stack of SaaS tools by the head. Workbooks is one nexus — add your whole company and the price doesn't move. Drag the slider.</p>
  
      <div class="cp-grid">
        <table class="cp-table">
          <thead><tr><th colspan="2">The usual stack</th><th class="num">/ user · mo</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="bc"><span class="g" data-brand="slack"></span>Slack</td><td class="mut">Chat</td><td class="num">$18</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="bc"><span class="g" data-brand="notion"></span>Notion</td><td class="mut">Docs</td><td class="num">$20</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="bc"><span class="g" data-brand="linear"></span>Linear</td><td class="mut">Project mgmt</td><td class="num">$16</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="bc"><span class="g" data-brand="retool"></span>Retool</td><td class="mut">Internal tools</td><td class="num">$20</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="bc"><span class="g" data-brand="vercel"></span>Vercel</td><td class="mut">Hosting</td><td class="num">$20</td></tr>
          </tbody>
          <tfoot><tr><td colspan="2">Per head, every head</td><td class="num">≈ $94</td></tr></tfoot>
        </table>
  
        <div class="cp-calc">
          <div class="cp-seats">
            <label for="seats">Your team — <b id="seatN">25</b> people</label>
            <input type="range" id="seats" min="1" max="500" value="25" step="1" aria-label="team size">
            <div class="cp-seatscale"><span>1</span><span>500</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="cp-bars">
            <div class="cp-bar stack">
              <div class="cp-bl"><span>The usual stack</span><span class="mut">scales per seat</span></div>
              <div class="cp-track"><i id="stackBar"></i><b id="stackCost">$2,350/mo</b></div>
            </div>
            <div class="cp-bar wb">
              <div class="cp-bl"><span>Workbooks</span><span class="mut">flat · every seat included</span></div>
              <div class="cp-track"><i id="wbBar"></i><b>from $29<span>/mo</span></b></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="cp-save">You save <b id="saveAmt">$2,321</b>/mo — the gap grows with every hire.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
  
      <table class="cp-tiers-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th class="num">Per month</th><th class="num">Storage</th><th class="num">Seats</th><th class="r">Built for</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="pn">Starter</td><td class="num">$29</td><td class="num">50 GB</td><td class="num inf">Unlimited</td><td class="r mut">A project or small team</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="pn">Team</td><td class="num">$99</td><td class="num">250 GB</td><td class="num inf">Unlimited</td><td class="r mut">A growing team</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="pn">Scale</td><td class="num">$249</td><td class="num">1 TB</td><td class="num inf">Unlimited</td><td class="r mut">Serious compute + storage</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="pn">Enterprise</td><td class="num">Custom</td><td class="num">Custom</td><td class="num inf">Unlimited</td><td class="r mut">SSO · SCIM · dedicated</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="cp-foot">Every tier carries <b>unlimited users + workspaces</b> — you scale one nexus by memory and bandwidth, never by headcount. <a href="https://app.workbooks.sh">Start building →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
end
